demy-id "q-99478" :question/problem "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{6}^{x}-4}{{3}^{x}+c}=4,$ what is the value of constant $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can evaluate this limit in terms of the constant $c$ using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{6}^{x}-4}{{3}^{x}+c} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({6}^{x}-4)}{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({3}^{x}+c)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{6}^{2}-4}{{3}^{2}+c} \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{9+c}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the above limit is equal to $4,$ we can equate the above with $4,$ and then solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{32}{9+c} & =4 \\\\ 9+c & =8 \\\\ c & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-99478/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58de617-785d-5318-9d12-99651e030eb2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99478"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339068/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "1daa7f40-2c49-5fa3-8437-18dfb24ce1f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339068/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c" :answer/id #uuid "7ee2e521-51c4-542b-9048-fa9e3fdecd1f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339068/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8394ae01-9999-5011-a442-3e3b60b55055" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339068/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-339068/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-339068/field-1/650efaaa01beaa7de6c030497edff1dd29c570bf683f3726bbcacabc3dfa7e4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339068" :question/id #uuid "a67fb5a2-d339-56cf-b965-422c99215cb0" :question/math-academy-id "q-339068" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}{4}^{x/2}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can evaluate this limit using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}{4}^{x/2} & ={4}^{2/2} \\\\  & ={4}^{1} \\\\  & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339068/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58de617-785d-5318-9d12-99651e030eb2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339068"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339038/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "7bd15216-9241-5437-87a5-7aa85fdcab4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339038/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "80c5c700-664e-540f-8ef2-d94ec6e8a84c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339038/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer-field/choices ["q-339038/field-1/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339038" :question/id #uuid "3510d7de-32fd-5111-93cc-455f85f59c80" :question/math-academy-id "q-339038" :question/problem "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{5}^{x}+c}{{2}^{x}-1}=4,$ what is the value of constant $c?$\n\n$c=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can evaluate this limit in terms of the constant $c$ using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{5}^{x}+c}{{2}^{x}-1} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 1}({5}^{x}+c)}{{lim}_{x\\to 1}({2}^{x}-1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{1}+c}{{2}^{1}-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+c}{2-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{5+c}{1} \\\\  & =5+c\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the above limit is equal to $4,$ we can equate the above with $4,$ and then solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5+c & =4 \\\\ c & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339038/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58de617-785d-5318-9d12-99651e030eb2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer/id #uuid "145665d3-c61d-546e-b2ac-b80b2d74c704" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "20125743-20cd-5880-b87f-4499df0b35a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "b978c8df-f569-5e2e-86c2-bd36ae1853c2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "d4e2cd67-6981-50a5-8092-60a3cfe6e363" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "6e4fff56-c8d2-5785-ad70-7aede08c2f1d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e7f24ad5-f310-5aa2-82b1-e6b69d72a35c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-67625/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" :answer-field/choices ["q-67625/selection/4de395131b8c6206950603752bf3404c42f4dd6f0a41fee38e42388d1b92c133" "q-67625/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-67625/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-67625/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-67625/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-67625" :question/id #uuid "b66a2bc7-58d6-5c40-a5fd-6a8dcb6c5064" :question/math-academy-id "q-67625" :question/problem "Given that ${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{4}^{x}-c}{3\\cdot {2}^{x}}=2$, what is the value of constant $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can evaluate this limit in terms of the constant $c$ using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{{4}^{x}-c}{3\\cdot {2}^{x}} & =\\frac{{4}^{0}-c}{3\\cdot {2}^{0}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-c}{3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the above limit is equal to $2,$ we can equate the above with $2,$ and then solve for $c:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1-c}{3} & =2 \\\\ 1-c & =6 \\\\ -c & =6-1 \\\\ c & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-67625/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58de617-785d-5318-9d12-99651e030eb2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-67625"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339070/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer/id #uuid "b22c97df-d833-5ca1-8878-d4d3b24e6516" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339070/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "20dcc540-a54a-5f42-85ad-e32a190fce5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339070/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a" :answer-field/choices ["q-339070/field-1/83c2285763389b0bc8b13e9777da06a48782d28e9c124603d3003cc4dc2e718a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339070" :question/id #uuid "9c1511ad-2957-5cf6-967e-dc706d69b890" :question/math-academy-id "q-339070" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{3}^{x}+5}{{2}^{x}-3}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can evaluate this limit using direct substitution, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{3}^{x}+5}{{2}^{x}-3} & =\\frac{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({3}^{x}+5)}{{lim}_{x\\to 2}({2}^{x}-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{2}+5}{{2}^{2}-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9+5}{4-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{1} \\\\  & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339070/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b58de617-785d-5318-9d12-99651e030eb2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339070"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-302435/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer/id #uuid "51e725ca-fd00-51ab-9408-80b5ef500b0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-302435/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6371c250-6d55-58ba-acec-66d4d7eb2325" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-302435/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c" :answer-field/choices ["q-302435/field-1/b67476ffce451bf9cc94e82f22f7f4f4b23075d2e02b9ea63c2ad56fd611692c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-302435" :question/id #uuid "e3419a6d-4719-5900-9c80-808b1ab34f75" :question/math-academy-id "q-302435" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(2\\cdot {5}^{x})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }(2\\cdot {5}^{x})=2\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the graph of $y={5}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943873/assets/02d46e13c84fc575f489a9870f3b1213eb3d180f3f5ef6e6a546d3acfe4b2282.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound  as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=\\infty .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{5}^{x}=2\\cdot \\infty =\\infty .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-302435/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae016162-6fee-5bb7-950f-fb7aa1ce4e11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-302435"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-54489/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "f1c9fb89-2c61-5534-8f76-3ed9ca135607" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54489/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "06056a1a-c82d-5a9a-a7d3-fe3650752a72" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54489/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "37b882d4-5743-5eb7-88f5-42e026a07f76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54489/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "045255a9-7499-5145-923d-7b483d71226e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54489/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "6ad1ce93-b73d-56ca-ac21-e0ff186b006d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-54489/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e33cedd1-640e-504d-b518-aba156b282a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-54489/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055c