es without bound as $x$ decreases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}=\\infty .\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-99505/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae016162-6fee-5bb7-950f-fb7aa1ce4e11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99505"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339406/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "393f08f1-3c62-5ef1-ba0c-b21b5ad7ed40" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339406/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "0556e7bb-aa73-5cc1-b118-289ddc1ea41e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339406/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "5a93e47a-a814-5dff-ae9d-c84009a5b465" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339406/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-339406/field-1/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-339406/field-1/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339406" :question/id #uuid "cdb890f6-825b-5339-a7fb-0c9b108e7781" :question/math-academy-id "q-339406" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the limit using the algebra of limits, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }-\\frac{5}{3}\\cdot {(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x} & =(-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we recall the graph of $y={(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943873/assets/9a249437f97a441c409b17e0f30a59bdcb70df02610f18d9320361d3d0d6708a.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function decreases to zero as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x}=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n(-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot {lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{2}{7})}^{x}=(-\\frac{5}{3})\\cdot 0=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339406/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ae016162-6fee-5bb7-950f-fb7aa1ce4e11"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-99507/selection/10293ac0295e0e79554137a949f5c5c46b9812dcc0a3ecb6349c4cb5e6acdff3" :answer/id #uuid "9e58bd00-d4b3-5998-8e73-f9d05a174913" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99507/selection/64ee21896e4acdba2b7ccd5d21e7c3b0caad319fb011e671d6ce72f671b3bb6c" :answer/id #uuid "9452706c-2fda-5cc8-8170-1cb2b017f46c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99507/selection/7bc54ef2cebd9c4cf6fef3072c83d13d0dfd6652d02cb9919fbcbc5497b7a408" :answer/id #uuid "1147d273-bca4-53e8-a661-1faed37b16d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99507/selection/6d8a7c7e73b503e82ee3fdeaeeda8131c0106d9ecb6a16ba218483b62acd0090" :answer/id #uuid "014c37cf-2a32-5a29-8ae8-ebe5dd4e16f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99507/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "d2d93252-eebd-567f-a35a-3eab753ef9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99507/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "326a7dae-860c-50cf-aaaf-22f8ee67a392" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct 